MINISTRY OF EARTH SCIENCES (MoES) — EXPEDITION REPORT
STATION: BHARATI STATION (LARSEMANN HILLS, ANTARCTICA)
COORDINATES: LAT -69.4°, LONG 76.2°
DISCIPLINE: OCEANOGRAPHY & MARINE SCIENCE

TITLE: Prydz Bay Oceanographic Stratification & Ice Shelf Basal Melting Rate
AUTHOR: Dr. Ananya Sharma & MoES Southern Ocean Team

ABSTRACT:
High-precision CTD hydrographic profiles collected near Larsemann Hills reveal seasonal intrusions of Modified Circumpolar Deep Water (MCDW) into the basal cavity of the Prydz Bay ice shelf. Thermal forcing accounts for an estimated 1.4 m/yr ice shelf basal melt rate.

KEY FINDINGS:
1. Warm intrusion of MCDW detected at 450m depth in Prydz Bay.
2. Basal melt rate accelerated by 14% compared to 2018 benchmark data.
3. Surface phytoplankton blooming correlates with increased glacial iron discharge.
